        "source": "thermodynamics-of-mind.pdf"
      },
      {
        "name": "Intrinsic Neural Timescales",
        "type": "Concept",
        "description": "The characteristic time windows over which neurons integrate information, key for input processing and shaping the hierarchy of neural dynamics as studied by Golesorkhi et al.",
        "tags": [],
        "created": "2026-05-29T23:41:01.690Z",
        "source": "thermodynamics-of-mind.pdf"
      },
      {
        "name": "Temporal Integration",
        "type": "Concept",
        "description": "The process by which the brain combines information over time, governed by intrinsic neural timescales to facilitate segregation and processing.",
        "tags": [],
        "created": "2026-05-29T23:41:01.837Z",
        "source": "thermodynamics-of-mind.pdf"
      },
      {
        "name": "Temporal Segregation",
        "type": "Concept",
        "description": "The process by which the brain distinguishes between different temporal inputs, working in conjunction with temporal integration as described by Wolff et al.",
