        "content": "Turbulence is not limited to fluid dynamics but is also observed in other physical systems, including coupled oscillators and, critically, the human brain. Recent studies have confirmed the presence of turbulence in brain dynamics, suggesting that neural systems operate within this same efficient, far-from-equilibrium regime.\n\nTurbulence is not limited to fluid dynamics but is also observed in other physical systems, including coupled oscillators and, critically, the human brain. Recent studies have confirmed the presence of turbulence in brain dynamics, suggesting that neural systems operate within this same efficient, far-from-equilibrium regime. When modeling the brain as a system of coupled oscillators, research shows that the level of turbulence varies significantly across different brain states. These variations have been documented in conditions such as different forms of coma, sleep states, and psychedelic experiences, indicating that turbulence is a dynamic marker of consciousness levels.",
