      {
        "content": "Using FDT in conjunction with a generative, perturbative whole-brain model allows for the estimation of FDT violation across different brain states. This approach can specifically analyze states such as wakefulness, cognitive tasks, and deep sleep, providing new insights into how thermodynamic balance shifts with consciousness levels.\n\nUsing FDT in conjunction with a generative, perturbative whole-brain model allows for the estimation of FDT violation across different brain states, including wakefulness, cognitive tasks, and deep sleep. This model-based approach surpasses model-free analyses of unperturbed states by actively simulating perturbations to reveal the underlying nonequilibrium dynamics, providing new insights into how thermodynamic balance shifts with consciousness levels.",
