      },
      {
        "content": "The framework utilizes Onsager’s regression principle to provide a simple derivation of the Fluctuation-Dissipation Theorem (FDT). This principle posits that the evolution of a system from an initial equilibrium state to a final equilibrium state, when driven by an external perturbation, can be treated mathematically as a spontaneous equilibrium fluctuation.",
