        "content": "The expanded Thermodynamics of Mind framework aims to shed new light on the orchestration and hierarchical organization of the brain in health, with the long-term goal of better understanding the leading breakdowns in neuropsychiatric diseases. By mapping healthy hierarchical dynamics, the framework seeks to identify specific thermodynamic deviations associated with pathological states.\n\nThe expanded Thermodynamics of Mind framework is not positioned as a complete general theory of brain function but as a significant step toward revealing the underlying principles of hierarchy that shape the nonequilibrium state of the human brain. It aims to shed new light on the orchestration and hierarchical organization of the brain in health, with the long-term goal of better understanding the leading breakdowns in neuropsychiatric diseases. The framework already demonstrates predictive power by mapping healthy hierarchical dynamics to identify specific thermodynamic deviations associated with pathological states.",
