      {
        "content": "G-Guzman, E. et al. (2023) identified that the lack of temporal brain dynamics asymmetry is a signature of impaired consciousness states, published in Interface Focus. This finding reinforces the concept that conscious awareness relies on a specific directional flow of time (arrow of time) in neural processing, and its absence correlates with pathological or reduced states of consciousness.",
