      {
        "content": "Killingsworth, M.A. and Gilbert, D.T. (2010) published the study 'A wandering mind is an unhappy mind' in Science, demonstrating a strong correlation between mind-wandering and decreased happiness. This reference suggests that the thermodynamic cost or inefficiency associated with the brain's default mode network and intrinsic dynamics may have direct phenomenological consequences for subjective well-being.",
