      {
        "content": "Shannon, C.E. (1948) published 'A mathematical theory of communication' in the Bell System Technical Journal, founding information theory. This classic work is cited to ground the framework's information-theoretic metrics, linking thermodynamic entropy to Shannon entropy and establishing the mathematical basis for quantifying information processing in the brain.",
