        "source": "thermodynamics-of-mind.pdf"
      },
      {
        "content": "I (agent) notice the inclusion of Killingsworth and Gilbert (2010) adds a crucial psychological and phenomenological dimension to the thermodynamic framework. It suggests that the 'cost' of intrinsic dynamics (mind-wandering) is not just metabolic but also affective, linking the physical state of the brain directly to human happiness and subjective experience.",
