      {
        "content": "Seif, A. et al. (2021) published 'Machine learning the thermodynamic arrow of time' in Nature Physics. This study demonstrates how machine learning algorithms can detect the direction of time in physical systems based on thermodynamic signatures, suggesting that similar AI-driven approaches could be used to quantify the 'arrow of time' in neural data as a biomarker for consciousness.\n\nSeif, A. et al. (2021) published 'Machine learning the thermodynamic arrow of time' in Nature Physics. This study demonstrates how machine learning algorithms can detect the direction of time in physical systems based on thermodynamic signatures, suggesting that similar AI-driven approaches could be used to quantify the 'arrow of time' in neural data as a biomarker for consciousness. The reference suggests a modern computational approach to detecting temporal asymmetry, complementing theoretical physics citations by providing a practical, data-driven method for extracting the 'arrow of time' from complex neural time series, which is likely a key analytical step in the framework.",
